# Jmix Enum Rules

## Scope
Applies to enums in `src/main/java/**/entity/`

## Enum Pattern
```java
public enum Status implements EnumClass<String> {
    VALUE("value_id");
    
    private final String id;
    
    Status(String id) { this.id = id; }
    
    @Override
    public String getId() { return id; }
    
    @Nullable
    public static Status fromId(String id) {
        for (Status s : values()) {
            if (s.getId().equals(id)) return s;
        }
        return null;
    }
}
```

## Required
- Implement `EnumClass<String>` or `EnumClass<Integer>`
- `getId()` method
- Static `fromId()` method with `@Nullable`

## Entity Usage
```java
@Column(name = "STATUS")
private String status;

public Status getStatus() {
    return status == null ? null : Status.fromId(status);
}

public void setStatus(Status status) {
    this.status = status == null ? null : status.getId();
}
```

## After Creating Enum
- Add messages for all values in `messages_en.properties`
- Liquibase: VARCHAR for String, INT for Integer

## Forbidden
- Plain enums without `EnumClass`
- Missing `fromId()` method
- Storing enum name directly
